<item>
            <title>[LU-20811] ptlrpc: ptlrpc_request_free() before pack leaks the import reference</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20811</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;ptlrpc_request_alloc() takes an import reference (class_import_get()) and increments&lt;br/&gt;
imp_reqs. ptlrpc_request_free() drops neither. If a caller frees the request before&lt;br/&gt;
ptlrpc_request_pack(), both leak. The import is then never destroyed and never goes idle.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20050&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: fix sepol error handling in ptlrpc_connect_import_locked&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20050&quot;&gt;LU-20050&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20546&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: import reference leaked or double-released on setup failure&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20546&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20546&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; fixed the sepol and pack-failure cases. Some pre-pack exits in&lt;br/&gt;
osc_brw_prep_request() still leak:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160; - the encryption folio array allocation, obd_pool_get_folios_array(), and the per-page&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; &#160; encryption failure&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - cl_env_get() failure&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - cl_object_attr_get() failure&lt;br/&gt;
&#160; - the -ENODATA exit for an empty RPC to an old server&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible fix: when rq_import is still set, let ptlrpc_request_free() itself decrement&lt;br/&gt;
imp_reqs and call class_import_put(). After &lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20546&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: import reference leaked or double-released on setup failure&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20546&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20546&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, a pack failure clears rq_import, so&lt;br/&gt;
callers that free after a failed pack stay correct. This needs an audit of all&lt;br/&gt;
ptlrpc_request_free() callers. It would also remove the open-coded put in&lt;br/&gt;
ptlrpc_request_alloc_internal().&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
Found during review of &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68582&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68582&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href=&quot;https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20546&quot; title=&quot;ptlrpc: import reference leaked or double-released on setup failure&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;LU-20546&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-20546&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;</description>
